{
  "id": "Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Sqlite",
  "name": "Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Sqlite",
  "area": "Data",
  "tagline": "SQLite implementation of **`IFileMetadataStore`** using Entity Framework Core. Functional parity with `Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Postgres` for embedded, offline-first, and local-dev scenarios.",
  "description": "SQLite implementation of **`IFileMetadataStore`** using Entity Framework Core. Functional parity with [\n`Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Postgres`](../Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Postgres/README.md) for embedded, offline-first, and local-dev scenarios.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register services",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "using Lyo.FileMetadataStore.Sqlite;\n\n// Simple\nservices.AddSqliteFileMetadataStore(\"Data Source=./filestore.db\");\n\n// With auto-migrations at host startup\nservices.AddSqliteFileMetadataStoreDbContextFactoryFromConfiguration(configuration);\nservices.AddSqliteFileMetadataStore();\nservices.AddSqliteFileAuditSink();\nservices.AddSqliteFileDownloadAccessService();\nservices.AddSqliteStagedFileUploadStore(); // optional — builder adds when missing\n\n// Keyed (multi-store hosts)\nservices.AddSqliteFileMetadataStoreKeyed(\"sqlite-metadata\")\n    .ConfigureSqliteFileStore(options => {\n        options.ConnectionString = \"Data Source=./filestore.db\";\n        options.EnableAutoMigrations = true;\n    })\n    .Build();"
    },
    {
      "title": "Register services (2)",
      "language": "json",
      "code": "{\n  \"SqliteFileMetadataStore\": {\n    \"ConnectionString\": \"Data Source=./filestore.db\",\n    \"EnableAutoMigrations\": true\n  }\n}"
    },
    {
      "title": "Register services (3)",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddS3FileStorageServiceKeyed(\"my-files\")\n    .UseFileMetadataStore(\"sqlite-metadata\")\n    .Build(configuration);"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "What is included",
      "headers": [
        "Component",
        "Role"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**`SqliteFileMetadataStore`**",
          "`IFileMetadataStore` + `IHealth`"
        ],
        [
          "**`SqliteFileAuditSink`**",
          "`IFileAuditEventHandler` — append-only audit rows"
        ],
        [
          "**`SqliteMultipartUploadSessionStore`**",
          "`IMultipartUploadSessionStore`"
        ],
        [
          "**`SqliteStagedFileUploadStore`**",
          "`IStagedFileUploadStore`"
        ],
        [
          "**`SqliteFileDownloadAccessService`**",
          "Time-boxed download access tokens"
        ],
        [
          "**`SqliteFileMetadataStoreDbContext`**",
          "EF Core context (6 tables, same shape as Postgres)"
        ]
      ],
      "trail": "Schema tables: `file_metadata`, `file_data`, `file_audit_events`, `multipart_upload_session`, `staged_file_upload`, `file_download_access_links`."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Registration",
      "text": "`appsettings.json`: Wire blob storage to the keyed metadata store the same way as Postgres:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Migrations",
      "text": "Migrations ship in this package. Enable **`EnableAutoMigrations`** (via [`Lyo.Sqlite`](../../Sqlite/Lyo.Sqlite/README.md)) or run `dotnet ef database update` using `SqliteFileMetadataStoreDbContextFactory`. Design-time connection string: `FILEMETADATASTORE_CONNECTION_STRING` or `FILESTORE_CONNECTION_STRING` (defaults to `Data Source=./filestore-design.db`)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Concurrency",
      "text": "SQLite is single-writer. Suitable for embedded clients, local tools, and low-concurrency dev hosts. For high-throughput multi-instance ingestion use Postgres. Enable WAL at the connection level if your host opens many concurrent readers (`PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL`)."
    }
  ],
